#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:1
msgid "# About Open Source"
msgstr "# 關於開放原始碼"

#. type: 註解
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:2
#: operation-templates/about/benefits.md:2
#: operation-templates/about/glossary.md:2
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:2
#: operation-templates/about/opensource-guide.md:2
#: operation-templates/about/ospo.md:2
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"########################################################################################\n"
"For OSPO Staff: How to Use This Template\n"
"\n"
"1. Replace placeholders in the body text like [Company Name] with your company information.\n"
"2. Verify completeness using the customization checklist.\n"
"3. Refer to the customization guide at the end to expand content based on your company's context.\n"
"\n"
"Simply replacing placeholders allows immediate use as internal documentation.\n"
"Expanding text according to the guide yields an even more practical document.\n"
"########################################################################################\n"
"-->"
msgstr ""
"<!--\n"
"########################################################################################\n"
"給 OSPO 承辦人：本範本的使用方式\n"
"\n"
"1. 將本文中的 [公司名稱] 等佔位符替換為自家公司資訊\n"
"2. 用客製化檢核清單確認沒有遺漏\n"
"3. 參考文末的客製化指南，依自家公司狀況增補內容\n"
"\n"
"只做佔位符替換也可以當作公司內部文件使用。\n"
"依指南增補內容後，可以做出更具實效性的版本。\n"
"########################################################################################\n"
"-->"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:3
msgid ""
"Today, virtually no enterprise operates without using open source software.\n"
"[Company Name] is no exception; most of the [primary utilization areas (e.g., web browsers, server software, development tools, cloud services, mobile applications)] we rely on daily operate using open source software."
msgstr ""
"如今，可說幾乎沒有任何企業是在完全不使用開放原始碼軟體的情況下營運的。\n"
"[公司名稱] 也不例外；包含日常使用的 [主要應用領域（例如：網頁瀏覽器、伺服器軟"
"體、開發工具、雲端服務及行動應用程式）]，大部分都是運用開放原始碼軟體來運作。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:4
msgid ""
"Originating from voluntary efforts by individual developers, open source software has broken through traditional limits of software development.\n"
"Software built solely by a single enterprise inevitably faces resource constraints, narrow perspectives, and innovation caps.\n"
"Open source provides a collaborative foundation where developers worldwide combine knowledge and experience through licensing frameworks that grant the freedom to use, modify, and distribute software."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼軟體源自個別開發者的自發投入，成為突破傳統軟體開發限制的創新做法。\n"
"單一企業或組織獨力開發軟體時，資源限制、觀點偏狹、創新速度受限等問題難以避免。\n"
"開放原始碼透過允許自由使用、修改與散布軟體的授權條款架構，提供了讓全世界開發者匯聚知識與經驗、共同協作的基礎。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:5
msgid ""
"In modern software, open source has established itself as core infrastructure.\n"
"[Representative OSS used internally (e.g., Linux operating systems power the vast majority of cloud infrastructure, Apache HTTP Server and Nginx serve numerous websites across the internet, and PostgreSQL and MySQL manage critical enterprise data globally)].\n"
"Without these technologies, maintaining modern digital infrastructure would be virtually impossible."
msgstr ""
"在現代軟體中，開放原始碼已確立其作為基礎技術的地位。\n"
"[自家公司使用的代表性 OSS（例如：Linux 作業系統支撐了大部分雲端基礎架構，Apache 網頁伺服器與 Nginx 驅動了網際網路上許多網站，PostgreSQL 與 MySQL 管理著全世界企業的重要資料）]。\n"
"可以說，沒有這些技術，現代數位社會將難以維持。"

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:6
msgid "## What Is the Essence of Open Source?"
msgstr "## 開放原始碼的本質是什麼？"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:7
msgid "Open Source Software (FOSS / OSS) refers to software whose creators grant permission for free use, modification, and distribution. The [Open Source Initiative (OSI)](https://opensource.org/) defines OSS as software licensed under terms meeting the [Open Source Definition (OSD)](https://opensource.org/osd). The OSD outlines 10 requirements, including free redistribution, source code access, and permission for derivative works. While this sounds like \"free software,\" \"free as in price\" (gratis) and \"free as in freedom\" (libre) are distinct concepts."
msgstr "開放原始碼軟體（英文：Free and Open Source Software，縮寫：OSS）指的是，經其開發者許可可以自由使用、修改與散布的軟體。[Open Source Initiative (OSI)](https://opensource.org/) 將其定義為符合「[開放原始碼定義](https://opensource.org/osd)」(Open Source Definition, OSD) 條件的授權條款，以及適用該授權條款的軟體。OSD 訂有再散布的自由、可取得原始碼、允許衍生作品等 10 項要求。這樣聽起來容易被理解為「可以免費使用的軟體」，但「free（免費）」與「free（自由）」是不同的概念。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:8
msgid ""
"Open source licenses serve as the formal mechanism conveying these freedoms to users.\n"
"Diverse licenses exist—such as MIT, Apache, and GPL—each specifying distinct rights grants and obligations, yet sharing the core principle of conferring software freedom.\n"
"These licenses balance protecting author rights while enabling software utilization and advancement."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼授權條款就是把這份自由明文化並授權給使用者的機制。\n"
"MIT、Apache、GPL 等各式授權條款並存，各自訂有不同的權利授予與條件，但在賦予自由這一點上是共通的。\n"
"這些授權條款在保護作者權利的同時，也提供了讓軟體能自由使用與發展的平衡。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:9
msgid ""
"The quality of open source software is sustained through project health and development transparency.\n"
"Code inspected by many eyes reveals bugs and security vulnerabilities faster, accelerating remediation.\n"
"Furthermore, deployment across diverse environments validates stability under varied conditions. This strength is summarized by Linus's Law: \"Given enough eyeballs, all bugs are shallow\" (Source: Raymond, Eric S. (1999). *The Cathedral and the Bazaar*)."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼軟體的品質，由其開發專案的健全性與透明度來確保。\n"
"被許多人盯著看的程式碼，比較容易發現程式錯誤與弱點，也比較容易被迅速修正。\n"
"此外，因為會在多樣環境中使用，各種條件下的運作都會被驗證，穩健性因此提升。\n"
"這正是開放原始碼的強項，也就是所謂「只要有足夠多的眼睛，所有的錯誤都會浮現（"
"Linus 定律）」（出處：Raymond, Eric S. (1999). *The Cathedral and the "
"Bazaar: Musings on Linux and Open Source by an Accidental Revolutionary*. "
"O'Reilly Media, Inc.）。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:10
msgid ""
"Open source communities serve not only technical development, but also knowledge sharing, mutual support, and continuous learning.\n"
"Developers worldwide collaborate to improve code, maintain documentation, and onboard users.\n"
"This synergy drives technological innovation beyond what any single company could achieve alone."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼社群不只是技術開發的場所，也是知識共享、相互支援與持續學習的場所。\n"
"全世界的開發者合作改善軟體、完善文件、支援新使用者。\n"
"透過這樣的協作，才可能達成個別企業獨力無法實現的技術創新水準。"

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:11
msgid "## How Open Source Works"
msgstr "## 開放原始碼如何運作"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:12
msgid ""
"Open source projects operate under decentralized development models.\n"
"In large-scale projects, rather than centralized management, maintainers direct project strategy while global contributors submit code improvements, bug fixes, and feature additions.\n"
"Platforms like GitHub and GitLab provide the technical infrastructure powering this distributed collaboration."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼專案以分散式的開發模式運作。\n"
"規模較大的專案並非中央集權式管理，而是由稱為維護者的負責人決定專案方向，全世界的貢獻者則進行程式碼改善、錯誤修正與新功能開發。\n"
"GitHub、GitLab 等平台提供支撐這種分散式開發的技術基礎。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:13
msgid ""
"The success of an open source project depends not only on technical excellence, but on community health.\n"
"Clear governance structures, constructive discussion cultures, welcoming environments for new contributors, and sustainable operations underpin long-term project viability."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼專案的成功不只取決於技術上的優秀，也取決於社群的健全性。\n"
"明確的治理架構、建設性的討論文化、歡迎新貢獻者的環境，以及可持續的營運體制，共同支撐專案的長期發展。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:14
msgid ""
"Enterprises leverage open source in diverse ways: consuming existing OSS directly, customizing code to internal requirements, publishing proprietary software as open source, or contributing back to upstream projects.\n"
"Each option presents distinct benefits and considerations requiring strategic evaluation."
msgstr ""
"企業運用開放原始碼的方式相當多樣。可以直接使用既有的開放原始碼軟體、依自家需"
"求加以修改、把自行開發的軟體以開放原始碼形式發佈、對開放原始碼專案貢獻等，選"
"項很多。\n"
"每種方式都有其效益與應考量之處，需要適切的策略判斷。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:15
msgid ""
"The open source ecosystem comprises diverse participants, including individual developers, enterprises, foundations, and academic institutions.\n"
"Organizations like the Apache Software Foundation, the Linux Foundation, and the Eclipse Foundation support governance and sustainability for key projects, enabling enterprises to depend on open source with confidence."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼生態系中有個人開發者、企業、基金會、學術機構等多樣的參與者。\n"
"Apache Software Foundation、Linux Foundation、Eclipse Foundation 等組織支援重要開放原始碼專案的治理與永續性。\n"
"因為有這些組織存在，企業才有能安心依賴開放原始碼的環境。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:16
msgid ""
"For modern enterprises, open source represents not just a technical choice, but the foundation for digital transformation.\n"
"Key emerging domains—such as [focused technical areas (e.g., cloud computing, artificial intelligence, big data, IoT, blockchain)]—advance rapidly by drawing upon open source project ecosystems.\n"
"Leveraging these technologies to secure competitive advantage requires deep understanding and strategic engagement with the open source ecosystem."
msgstr ""
"對現代企業而言，開放原始碼不只是技術選項，更成為數位轉型的基礎。\n"
"[自家公司投注的技術領域（例如：雲端運算、人工智慧、大數據、物聯網、區塊鏈）] 等許多最新技術，都大量借助開放原始碼專案的力量而發展。\n"
"若要運用這些技術取得競爭優勢，理解並適切運用開放原始碼生態系可說相當重要。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:17
msgid ""
"Beyond accelerating technical innovation, open source democratizes technology access.\n"
"Sharing advanced software globally enables technical advancement transcending geographical and economic constraints.\n"
"By participating in and contributing to this ecosystem, [Company Name] fulfills both engineering growth and corporate responsibility."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼不只加速技術創新，也推動知識的民主化。\n"
"優秀的軟體技術在全世界共享，讓超越地理與經濟限制的技術發展成為可能。\n"
"[公司名稱] 作為這個生態系的一份子參與並貢獻，就能同時實現技術成長與社會責任。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/about-opensource.md:18
msgid ""
"Leveraging open source at [Company Name] is not merely a cost-reduction tactic.\n"
"It represents a strategic investment yielding multifaceted value, including [desired values from OSS adoption (e.g., fostering innovation, upgrading engineering skills, recruiting top talent, establishing technical brand reputation)].\n"
"By managing open source under appropriate governance and risk management, we build sustainable technical competitive advantages.\n"
"For specific benefits, see [Benefits of Open Source](../about/benefits.md)."
msgstr ""
"[公司名稱] 運用開放原始碼並不只是降低成本的手段。\n"
"而是能提供 [自家公司希望從 OSS 運用中獲得的價值（例如：促進創新、提升技術人員技能、吸引優秀人才、建立技術品牌）] 等多面向價值的策略性投資。\n"
"在適切的治理與風險管理之下運用開放原始碼，就能建立可持續的技術競爭優勢。\n"
"關於具體效益，請參閱[開放原始碼的效益](../about/benefits.md)。"

