#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:1
msgid "# What Is InnerSource?"
msgstr "# 什麼是內源？"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:3
msgid ""
"InnerSource refers to the practice of applying open source development methodologies and culture to internal software development.\n"
"At [Company Name], we refer to this initiative as \"[Internal Name for InnerSource (e.g., InnerSource, Internal Source Code Sharing Initiative)].\""
msgstr ""
"內源 (InnerSource) 指的是把開放原始碼所累積的開發方法與實踐做法，導入公司內部軟體開發的一種取徑。\n"
"[公司名稱] 把這項作為稱為「[內源的公司內部稱法（例如：內源、原始碼公司內部公開活動）]」。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:4
msgid "Crucially, InnerSource is not merely a mechanism for code sharing; **it serves as an organizational foundation for developing the culture and skills required to master open source and contribute upstream externally.** Even for proprietary codebases that cannot be open-sourced publicly, InnerSource enables teams to reap open-source-style benefits through internal sharing and collaboration."
msgstr "重點在於，內源不只是共享程式碼的機制，而是**為了在公司內部培養能熟練運用開放原始碼、並進而延伸到對外貢獻的文化與技能的基礎**。即使是難以對外公開的程式碼，也能透過公司內部的共享與協作享有開放原始碼式的好處。"

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:5
msgid "## Why InnerSource Is Necessary"
msgstr "## 為什麼需要內源"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:6
msgid "Even when an internal team builds outstanding software, **the organization must understand and practice open source development culture and workflows** to sustain continuous improvements and eventually publish code as open source."
msgstr "即使公司內部開發出很棒的軟體，若要持續改善它、並在未來以開放原始碼形式發佈，**整個組織理解並能實踐開放原始碼開發方法與文化的體制**不可或缺。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:7
msgid ""
"Open source culture is not just a technical skill; it is an organizational capability shaping workflows and decision-making processes.\n"
"Simply releasing code publicly does not guarantee open source success. Without core values like **transparency, collaboration, and continuous improvement** deeply rooted in the organization, open source benefits remain unrealized, and public releases may introduce organizational risk."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼文化不只是技術技能，也是牽涉組織工作方式與決策流程的「文化能力 (cultural capability)」。\n"
"並不是「只要公開程式碼，開放原始碼就會成功」；若**透明、協作、持續改善**這些價值觀沒有在組織中扎根，就無法獲得開放原始碼的真正效益，發佈開放原始碼甚至可能對組織構成風險。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:8
msgid ""
"InnerSource **refers to applying open source principles and practices within an organization, primarily to foster cross-team collaboration and code sharing.**\n"
"In this context, InnerSource acts as a \"safe internal sandbox\" for cultivating these organizational capabilities, delivering the following benefits:"
msgstr ""
"內源指的是**主要為促進團隊之間的協作與程式碼共享，而在組織內部套用開放原始碼原則與實踐做法。**\n"
"在這個脈絡下，內源扮演的是培養這些組織能力的「安全的公司內部實驗場」角色。\n"
"藉此可以期待以下效果："

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:9
msgid "1. **Pathways to Open Source Maturity**"
msgstr "1. **通往開放原始碼的路徑**"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:10
msgid ""
"   InnerSource provides a natural evolution path toward open source maturity.\n"
"   Engineers master essential open source practices—such as code reviews, issue tracking, CI/CD, documentation, and community facilitation—within a safe internal environment.\n"
"   Through this journey, employees adopt open source mindsets centered on transparent problem solving, constructive feedback, and continuous learning.\n"
"   Ultimately, this experience translates into external contributions, enhancing corporate engineering prestige and recruiting power."
msgstr ""
"   內源提供組織在開放原始碼運用上邁向成熟的自然成長路徑。\n"
"   程式碼審查、Issue 管理、CI/CD、文件撰寫、社群運作等開放原始碼所需的技能，都能在安全的內部環境中學會。\n"
"   在這個過程中，員工會養成透明的問題解決、建設性回饋、持續學習等開放原始碼式的思維。\n"
"   最終，這些經驗會延伸為對外部開放原始碼專案的貢獻，有助於提升組織的技術評價與吸引人才。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:11
msgid "2. **Improved Engineering Efficiency**"
msgstr "2. **提升開發效率**"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:12
msgid ""
"    Traditional hierarchical management introduces buffer delays at organizational layers, constraining engineering agility.\n"
"    InnerSource flips this structure, empowering individuals closest to problems to solve them directly.\n"
"    Furthermore, sharing tools, libraries, and knowledge across business units unlocks synergies impossible within isolated silos.\n"
"    Organizations realize that code and knowledge are assets whose value multiplies through sharing rather than hoarding."
msgstr ""
"   在傳統的層級式管理中，需求穿過每一層時都會累積緩衝時間，最後壓力落到工程師身上。\n"
"   內源翻轉了這個結構，讓最貼近問題的人可以直接動手解決。\n"
"   此外，透過在組織內共享工具、程式庫與知識，會產生各自為政（穀倉效應）時無法實現的相乘效果。\n"
"   整個組織會逐漸理解，程式碼與知識資產是共享比圈占更能增值的資源。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:13
msgid "3. **Accelerated Innovation**"
msgstr "3. **加速創新**"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:14
msgid ""
"    InnerSource creates a continuous value-creation ecosystem.\n"
"    Teams act as both consumers and contributors—leveraging components built by other units while contributing bug fixes and features back—elevating overall organizational engineering capability.\n"
"    This environment of circulating knowledge, mutual technology advancement, and talent growth establishes sustainable competitive advantages beyond individual project successes."
msgstr ""
"   內源會建立持續創造價值的生態系。\n"
"   各團隊同時擔任使用者與貢獻者，一邊運用其他團隊的元件，一邊把改良與新功能回饋回去，整個組織的技術水準因而提升。\n"
"   在知識循環、技術相互發展與人才成長彼此促進的環境中，能建立超越個別專案成功的長期競爭優勢。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:15
msgid "4. **Transformed Organizational Culture**"
msgstr "4. **改善組織文化**"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:16
msgid ""
"    InnerSource creates organic transparency and dissolves departmental silos.\n"
"    An open corporate culture where information flows naturally fosters a supportive work environment, boosting developer satisfaction and talent retention."
msgstr ""
"   內源會自然而然創造透明度，消除部門之間的穀倉。\n"
"   在資訊自然流通的開放組織文化下，能培養出互相支援的職場環境，進而提升工程師的滿意度與人才留任率。"

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:17
msgid "## Cultivating Open Source Culture Internally"
msgstr "## 為了讓開放原始碼文化在公司內部扎根"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:18
msgid ""
"Rooting open source culture internally requires understanding and practicing the four core principles of InnerSource, while maintaining clarity on what InnerSource is not.\n"
"This section outlines these four principles alongside common misconceptions."
msgstr ""
"要讓開放原始碼文化在公司內部扎根，理解並實踐以下內源的四項原則相當重要。\n"
"另一方面，也需要明確「什麼不是內源」。\n"
"本小節將說明內源的四項原則，以及不屬於內源的情況。"

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:19
msgid "### The Four Principles of InnerSource"
msgstr "### 內源的四項原則"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:20
msgid "Adopting these four core open source cultural values internally is essential for InnerSource—and ultimately open source—success:"
msgstr "把開放原始碼的以下四種文化導入公司內部，是內源成功、進而是開放原始碼成功的關鍵。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:21
msgid ""
"1. **Openness**\n"
"   Source code is open internally across the organization for anyone to read and learn from.\n"
"   Developers inspect and learn from code written by other teams, spurring cross-pollination of knowledge and elevating skill levels across the company."
msgstr ""
"1. **Openness（開放）**\n"
"   原始碼在組織內公開，任何人都能自由存取。\n"
"   這讓開發者能參考並學習其他團隊的程式碼，使知識共享更活躍，帶動整體技能提升。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:22
msgid ""
"2. **Transparency**\n"
"   Beyond code, decision-making processes and discussions are conducted openly.\n"
"   Transparent governance enables external developers to participate easily, transforming software into a shared organizational asset."
msgstr ""
"2. **Transparency（透明）**\n"
"   不只是程式碼，討論過程也公開。也就是說，決策是如何做出的都是透明的。\n"
"   這讓其他團隊的開發者容易參與，專案也會被視為整個組織的共享資產。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:23
msgid ""
"3. **Prioritized Mentorship**\n"
"    Maintainers prioritize support for guest contributors to lower friction for new developers.\n"
"    Active mentorship encourages continuous incoming contributions across organizational boundaries."
msgstr ""
"3. **Prioritized Mentorship（優先的指導）**\n"
"    為了讓新開發者容易參與，會優先提供支援。\n"
"    透過跟進客座團隊的貢獻、降低參與門檻，專案就會持續產生新的貢獻。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:24
msgid ""
"4. **Voluntary Code Contribution**\n"
"    Contributions to projects are never forced.\n"
"    Assistance from maintainers is likewise voluntary. Teams collaborate respectfully as equal peers to advance engineering goals."
msgstr ""
"4. **Voluntary Code Contribution（自發的程式碼貢獻）**\n"
"    對專案的貢獻不是被強制的。\n"
"    專案提供的支援也是自發的。各團隊彼此尊重、互相合作，推進開發。"

#. type: 標題
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:25
msgid "### What InnerSource Is Not"
msgstr "### 什麼不是內源"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:26
msgid "To build a healthy open source culture, avoid these common misconceptions. Cultivating proper understanding directly underpins open source success:"
msgstr ""
"要讓開放原始碼文化在公司內部扎根，避免以下誤解也很重要。\n"
"在組織中培養這樣的文化，會直接帶動開放原始碼運用的成功。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:27
msgid ""
"1. **Personal Hobbies**\n"
"   InnerSource is not an unstructured activity for personal amusement.\n"
"   It does not mean writing code based solely on personal interest; projects must serve broader organizational needs.\n"
"   Sharing and collaboration aim to maximize enterprise value."
msgstr ""
"1. **為個人目的的活動**\n"
"   內源不是為個人目的而做的活動。\n"
"   也就是說，內源不是依特定個人的興趣去寫程式碼的活動。\n"
"   它必須回應整個組織的需求。\n"
"   共享與協作應以提高整個組織的價值為目的。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:28
msgid ""
"2. **Individual Ownership**\n"
"    Deliverables are not individual property.\n"
"    InnerSource is not simply publishing personal code to colleagues.\n"
"    Code represents a corporate asset managed transparently for collective benefit."
msgstr ""
"2. **產出物歸個人所有**\n"
"    產出物不是個人的所有物。\n"
"    也就是說，內源不是把個人寫的程式碼單純公開給他人看的活動。\n"
"    程式碼是整個組織的資產，應以任何人都能存取的形式管理。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:29
msgid ""
"3. **Universal Ownership (\"Everyone Owns It\")**\n"
"    Deliverables are not owned by \"everyone.\" The \"everyone owns it\" mindset dilutes accountability.\n"
"    As in open source, designated maintainer teams retain ownership, driving code quality and architectural direction. This is termed \"Weak Ownership.\""
msgstr ""
"3. **所有人共同擁有程式碼**\n"
"    產出物也不是所有人的所有物。「所有人共同擁有」的想法有責任歸屬不明的風險。\n"
"    要像開放原始碼一樣，由適當擔任「維護者」的團隊負起責任，維持程式碼的品質與方向。\n"
"    這稱為「Weak Ownership（弱所有權）」。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:30
msgid ""
"4. **Dumping Code on Other Teams**\n"
"    InnerSource is not \"dumping unwanted code on neighboring teams.\"\n"
"    Teams leverage components based on genuine need and contribute back as appropriate, without obligation or coercion."
msgstr ""
"4. **強推給鄰近團隊**\n"
"    內源不是「把程式碼強推給鄰近團隊」的活動。\n"
"    各團隊依自己的需求使用程式碼，並依需要進行貢獻。\n"
"    對其他團隊沒有強制或義務。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:31
msgid ""
"5. **Publishing All Code**\n"
"    InnerSource does not mean opening every line of code internally.\n"
"    Teams distinguish between shareable assets and restricted code, governing repositories appropriately based on business requirements."
msgstr ""
"5. **公開所有程式碼**\n"
"    內源不是公開所有程式碼的活動。\n"
"    也就是說，內源不是「把所有程式碼都在公司內部公開」的活動。\n"
"    要區分該共享與不該共享的程式碼，依商業需求適切管理。"

#. type: 引用
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:32
msgid ""
"> **Caution: Cross-Organizational Code Sharing and Licensing**\n"
"> Even within an InnerSource context, sharing code containing OSS across separate legal entities—such as subsidiaries, affiliates, overseas units, or partner firms—may legally constitute \"distribution.\" What appears to be internal sharing may be construed legally as distribution. When sharing code across organizational boundaries, consult Tax and Legal teams to establish compliant licensing policies."
msgstr ""
"> **注意：跨組織的程式碼共享與授權條款**\n"
"> 即使在內源的脈絡下，只要在子公司、關係企業、海外據點、合作夥伴企業等法人格不同的組織之間共享含 OSS 的程式碼，在授權條款上就可能構成「散布」。有些情況看似公司內部使用，法律上卻被解釋為散布，因此跨越組織界線共享時，請依需要與稅務或法務諮詢，並制定適切的授權政策，這相當重要。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:33
msgid ""
"6. **Uncontrolled Modification**\n"
"    InnerSource is not uncontrolled modification where anyone refactors code at will.\n"
"    Teams consume and modify code based on deliberate project needs through maintainer code reviews."
msgstr ""
"6. **任何人都能自由修改**\n"
"    內源不是任何人都能自由修改的活動。\n"
"    也就是說，內源不是「大家都變成組織內的個人開發者，想怎麼開發就怎麼開發、自由修改」這種事。\n"
"    各團隊依自己的需求使用程式碼，並依需要進行修改。\n"
"    對其他團隊沒有強制或義務。"

#. type: 段落
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:34
msgid "For case studies and patterns, consult the [InnerSource Commons Foundation](https://innersourcecommons.org/) and [InnerSource Patterns](https://patterns.innersourcecommons.org/)."
msgstr "關於案例與成功實例，請參閱 [InnerSource Commons Foundation](https://innersourcecommons.org/)；更具體的實踐做法則可參考[內源模式 (InnerSource Patterns)](https://patterns.innersourcecommons.org/)。"

#. type: 清單
#: operation-templates/about/innersource.md:38
msgid ""
"- [ ] Replaced all instances of [Company Name] with actual company name.\n"
"- [ ] Replaced [Internal Name for InnerSource] with actual internal naming (or chose to use \"InnerSource\").\n"
"- [ ] Documented concrete touchpoints with existing knowledge-sharing initiatives.\n"
"- [ ] Positioned phased InnerSource implementation within the OSPO roadmap.\n"
"- [ ] Identified pilot project candidates (or documented plans to identify them)."
msgstr ""
"- [ ] 已將所有 [公司名稱] 替換為自家公司名稱\n"
"- [ ] 已把 [內源的公司內部稱法] 換成自家公司的說法（或已決定直接沿用「內源」）\n"
"- [ ] 已具體寫出與既有知識管理活動的銜接點\n"
"- [ ] 已在 OSPO 活動的路線圖中安排內源的分階段導入計畫\n"
"- [ ] 已找出試行專案的候選（或已寫出找出候選的計畫）"

